{
    "description": "Lines across the view at pitch 80, alternating solid and dashed, styled 0.5 px on the left half and 1.5 px on the right. Pitch foreshortens every line below a device pixel. Lines styled under 1 px are meant to be hairlines and stay faint, so they are never widened; the 1.5 px lines are widened to stay visible. Each 0.5 px line either clearly covers a pixel row centre or lies clearly between two rows, so whether it is drawn does not depend on how a GPU rounds sub-pixel geometry. Each line layer is drawn three times so the faint coverage compounds into pixel values large enough for the image comparison to register.",
